(656847, 64891, 6999, '<td valign="top">Yep, it''s a car up in the air ... not meaning to be rude :-) Apart from that, there''s not a great deal I like here: the truck is slightly blurred, suggesting you didn''t quite have a quick enough shutter, yet you haven''t followed it to produce a blurred background and give any sensation of movement.</td>', 'Yep, it''s a car up in the air ... not meaning to be rude :-) Apart from that, there''s not a great deal I like here: the truck is slightly blurred, suggesting you didn''t quite have a quick enough shutter, yet you haven''t followed it to produce a blurred background and give any sensation of movement.', '2004-04-07 08:16:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(656849, 67729, 6999, '<td valign="top">Nice portrait - like the colour contrast here with the reflected sky. I would personally have cloned out the glass mark bottom left ... I keep trying to read what it says, and can''t, quite.</td>', 'Nice portrait - like the colour contrast here with the reflected sky. I would personally have cloned out the glass mark bottom left ... I keep trying to read what it says, and can''t, quite.', '2004-04-07 08:19:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(656852, 67521, 6999, '<td valign="top">Good toning - there''s a serenity to those tones of brown and grey - and a smoothness that''s appropriate to product photography, especially perfume. can''t say that I find iit to be anything out of the ordinary, though.</td>', 'Good toning - there''s a serenity to those tones of brown and grey - and a smoothness that''s appropriate to product photography, especially perfume. can''t say that I find iit to be anything out of the ordinary, though.', '2004-04-07 08:20:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(656854, 66993, 6999, '<td valign="top">I''m not certain that the colour noise is effective, certainly in such a near black and white shot. The capture is good, the scene is good, and it''s well composed however ... a decent photojournalism shot. Porcessing is lacking to my view though - the figure seems overly lightened, without putting back any contrast much, and as I said the noise (which doesn''t work like grain for me, being colour noise).</td>', 'I''m not certain that the colour noise is effective, certainly in such a near black and white shot. The capture is good, the scene is good, and it''s well composed however ... a decent photojournalism shot. Porcessing is lacking to my view though - the figure seems overly lightened, without putting back any contrast much, and as I said the noise (which doesn''t work like grain for me, being colour noise).', '2004-04-07 08:23:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(656857, 65076, 6999, '<td valign="top">Good crisp detailing, composition, focus etc. I find it lacking in any sense of drama though - the colouring is a touch too weak for that ... I think perhaps richer tones in the grases, and even darkening the sky further might have been effective. Either that or take it to black and white, to emphasise the cilhouette of the tree further. Competent shot, though.</td>', 'Good crisp detailing, composition, focus etc. I find it lacking in any sense of drama though - the colouring is a touch too weak for that ... I think perhaps richer tones in the grases, and even darkening the sky further might have been effective. Either that or take it to black and white, to emphasise the cilhouette of the tree further. Competent shot, though.', '2004-04-07 08:25:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(656860, 65258, 6999, '<td valign="top">Such a small image ... a shame perhaps, especially when the amount of compression artefacts present. Looks like it might have been intersting tonally, on those wall panels, but it''s really so little bigger than a thumbnail it''s impossible to tell.</td>', 'Such a small image ... a shame perhaps, especially when the amount of compression artefacts present. Looks like it might have been intersting tonally, on those wall panels, but it''s really so little bigger than a thumbnail it''s impossible to tell.', '2004-04-07 08:27:48.000000', NULL, 1),
