(658966, 65592, 7778, '<td valign="top">I can see how some would vote 2 and 3. I can easily see a vote of 6 - 10. But fifty-three 5''s?<br/>It''s funny, sad and odd, how a photograph which excites some of us is ''averaged'' by so many.<br/>Among your best, IMHO.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-04-08 00:20:17.</i></td>', 'I can see how some would vote 2 and 3. I can easily see a vote of 6 - 10. But fifty-three 5''s?It''s funny, sad and odd, how a photograph which excites some of us is ''averaged'' by so many.Among your best, IMHO.', '2004-04-08 01:18:28.000000', '2004-04-08 01:20:17.000000', 0),
(658967, 64384, 18737, '<td valign="top">Congratulations, amazing photography.</td>', 'Congratulations, amazing photography.', '2004-04-08 01:18:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(658969, 64157, 16301, '<td valign="top">Thanks to everyone for their comments, I''m glad you liked the photo.<br/> <br/>A larger version of it can be found <a href="//www.deviantart.com/view/5775777/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">here</a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-04-08 01:53:44.</i></td>', 'Thanks to everyone for their comments, I''m glad you liked the photo. A larger version of it can be found here', '2004-04-08 01:19:24.000000', '2004-04-08 02:53:44.000000', 0),
(658973, 67761, 13136, '<td valign="top">I liked this shot a lot. Gave it an 8. I thought for sure it would finish in the top 10. Good work.</td>', 'I liked this shot a lot. Gave it an 8. I thought for sure it would finish in the top 10. Good work.', '2004-04-08 01:21:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(658975, 66886, 16829, '<td valign="top">I want thank everyone for their comments on this one. And also ask some advice from more experienced photogs. The problem here was shooting directly at a street light. In order to keep the center from being totally blown out, I lost a lot of detail at the edges. The original shot was rather painterly looking, likely because of a Vivid color setting. Then when I brought out the darker areas, there was a lot of noise. The addition of noise reduction and some blurring ( the first two steps in any "painting" filter) brought out that aspect more. But I still liked the picture. Attached is the original. Any advice on how I could have captured a better shot to begin with?<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=68934" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/16829/thumb/68934.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/16829/thumb/68934.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/16829/thumb/68934.jpg"/></a></td>', 'I want thank everyone for their comments on this one. And also ask some advice from more experienced photogs. The problem here was shooting directly at a street light. In order to keep the center from being totally blown out, I lost a lot of detail at the edges. The original shot was rather painterly looking, likely because of a Vivid color setting. Then when I brought out the darker areas, there was a lot of noise. The addition of noise reduction and some blurring ( the first two steps in any "painting" filter) brought out that aspect more. But I still liked the picture. Attached is the original. Any advice on how I could have captured a better shot to begin with?', '2004-04-08 01:22:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(658981, 65453, 18737, '<td valign="top">Congratulations.</td>', 'Congratulations.', '2004-04-08 01:24:41.000000', NULL, 0),
