(659035, 67447, 18913, '<td valign="top">The people don''t understand what their supposed to be focusing on are essentially photography''s version of trailer trash.  These people have no imagination nor sensitivity.  They simply regurgitate the images that they have already seen a million times.  I loved your photo.  I don''t think people realize how difficult it is to pull off such a photo and how interesting it is and how it goes beyond pictures of a bird with a beak and into the realm of fine art.  It is something that is to be appreciated and taken in small sips, like the finest of wines.  Congratulations once again for such a fine work of ART.</td>', 'The people don''t understand what their supposed to be focusing on are essentially photography''s version of trailer trash.  These people have no imagination nor sensitivity.  They simply regurgitate the images that they have already seen a million times.  I loved your photo.  I don''t think people realize how difficult it is to pull off such a photo and how interesting it is and how it goes beyond pictures of a bird with a beak and into the realm of fine art.  It is something that is to be appreciated and taken in small sips, like the finest of wines.  Congratulations once again for such a fine work of ART.', '2004-04-08 01:54:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(659042, 64384, 9906, '<td valign="top">I have very mixed feelings on this one leaning towards the negative.  However I must give you credit for making me think about it as much as you did.  Somewhere between this version and the original is perfection...]<br/> <br/>Anyways, congrats on the ribbon!  Like Pits said, the majority rules.<br/>TC<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-04-08 00:59:56.</i></td>', 'I have very mixed feelings on this one leaning towards the negative.  However I must give you credit for making me think about it as much as you did.  Somewhere between this version and the original is perfection...] Anyways, congrats on the ribbon!  Like Pits said, the majority rules.TC', '2004-04-08 01:58:27.000000', '2004-04-08 01:59:56.000000', 0),
