(659603, 65815, 4564, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for the nice comments.  Once again, I find myself in 4th position. Ahhhhhhhh, the irony!  ;-) <br/> <br/>I salute the top 3 winners! Congrats!<br/> <br/>Kosmik: your joke/observation is hilarious!  By a feather... or two!  Man, that one cracks me up!!!!!!!!<br/> <br/>To answer some questions:<br/>- I called the shot Mirage because it was photographed at Dry Lake Mirage.  <br/>- Yeah, multiple 1''s and 2''s suck, but I have learned on DPC that the low votes are innevitable as soon as your shot contains any type of nudity.  That is the cost to pay to enter such an image in a challenge.  Doesn''t mean I don''t find it frustrating though.<br/>- Ursula: pount taken. The dust should go.<br/> <br/>Tahnks again all!  Keep shooting! <br/>See ya.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-04-08 14:16:25.</i></td>', 'Thank you all for the nice comments.  Once again, I find myself in 4th position. Ahhhhhhhh, the irony!  ;-)  I salute the top 3 winners! Congrats! Kosmik: your joke/observation is hilarious!  By a feather... or two!  Man, that one cracks me up!!!!!!!! To answer some questions:- I called the shot Mirage because it was photographed at Dry Lake Mirage.  - Yeah, multiple 1''s and 2''s suck, but I have learned on DPC that the low votes are innevitable as soon as your shot contains any type of nudity.  That is the cost to pay to enter such an image in a challenge.  Doesn''t mean I don''t find it frustrating though.- Ursula: pount taken. The dust should go. Tahnks again all!  Keep shooting! See ya.', '2004-04-08 13:44:53.000000', '2004-04-08 15:16:25.000000', 0),
