(660155, 65815, 19785, '<td valign="top">I love this picture! The Blue sky, the off centered hill, and the model, great job picking a red head for this one. Any other hair color would of not looked as good. She really does look like a mirage, from heaven! Congrates!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-04-08 19:29:08.</i></td>', 'I love this picture! The Blue sky, the off centered hill, and the model, great job picking a red head for this one. Any other hair color would of not looked as good. She really does look like a mirage, from heaven! Congrates!', '2004-04-08 20:27:26.000000', '2004-04-08 20:29:08.000000', 0),
(660291, 64270, 2310, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments everyone!  I <i>was</i> trying to focus your attention on the face and eyes through the direction of the frogs body, leaf placement, and depth of field.  I think that the slightly brighter level in the upper left corner does pull one''s eyes away.  It was fun and my best rated photo yet!  <br/> <br/>I would like to see more of these longer challanges as I really do not have the time during the week to participate in the weekly challanges as much...<br/> <br/>Oh, if you are interested...the common name of this frog is the "Tiger-Legged Monkey Frog" or the "Barred Leaf Frog".  They are not poisonous and use their brightly colored flash markings to attempt to startle any would be predators...<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-04-08 20:35:33.</i></td>', 'Thanks for the comments everyone!  I was trying to focus your attention on the face and eyes through the direction of the frogs body, leaf placement, and depth of field.  I think that the slightly brighter level in the upper left corner does pull one''s eyes away.  It was fun and my best rated photo yet!   I would like to see more of these longer challanges as I really do not have the time during the week to participate in the weekly challanges as much... Oh, if you are interested...the common name of this frog is the "Tiger-Legged Monkey Frog" or the "Barred Leaf Frog".  They are not poisonous and use their brightly colored flash markings to attempt to startle any would be predators...', '2004-04-08 21:33:45.000000', '2004-04-08 21:35:33.000000', 0),
(660294, 66535, 11793, '<td valign="top">well done.</td>', 'well done.', '2004-04-08 21:37:15.000000', NULL, 0),
