(661399, 66961, 18419, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments! I know that the clouds were overexposed (the sun was right behind the top of the pole), but I thought it ''worked'', especially in contrast to the deep focus and the dark earth tones of the pole.  I''ll try it again with a late afternoon sun and puffy clouds to see what that does.  Thanks again!<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/>Stu<br/></td>', 'Thanks for all the comments! I know that the clouds were overexposed (the sun was right behind the top of the pole), but I thought it ''worked'', especially in contrast to the deep focus and the dark earth tones of the pole.  I''ll try it again with a late afternoon sun and puffy clouds to see what that does.  Thanks again! CheersStu', '2004-04-09 22:45:00.000000', NULL, 0),
